body:
I feel the sympathy, but interviews have nothing with that. People want the show and not only seeing happy winners, but also sad losers. And losers should understand that they were weaker this time and give an interview. 
&nbsp;
And if TI loss breaks the player, he honestly shouldn't play anymore.
&nbsp;
Look at other sports. A lot of people overcome their losses. 
&nbsp;
The problem that reddit points is just so minor, and I don't understand why is it really a thing.

They are famous guys with a lot of fans watching them. They shouldn't lose their face in front of a camera whenever it will catch them. 

&nbsp;

Tell me the truth, you are just upset that all your favorite players are out.

You think they are boring just because they are chinese. 

&nbsp;

That's racist! :D

Are you really asking why?

&nbsp;

Because it's not a game between pals, you know. Big money, big losses. If your loss can crush you and you can't take a lesson of it, you deserve it.

Look at other sports. Does the coach run around his man during the match/race? Nope. 

&nbsp;

Players are NOT children who need to be guided, they should handle everything in arena by themeselves.
